00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:29,420
Now, when it comes to attribution inside of Meta, there are basically three now types of attributions that you can select.

231
00:22:29,420 --> 00:22:33,240
And just so you know, the attribution does two things for your business.

232
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:37,520
The first thing that it does is it actually tells Meta how to report data.

233
00:22:37,820 --> 00:22:46,560
So, if you tell Meta, "Hey, show me anybody who clicked an ad and purchased within 7 days," we'll get a purchase reported into Meta for you to see, okay?

234
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:50,340
The second thing that it does is that's also how Meta learns who to go after.

235
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:56,220
So, it's going to optimize basically for people who are going to purchase within a 7-day window, okay?

236
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:59,040
And so, this is where another bit of a topic comes up,

237
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:03,380
because as you can see here, there is two different attribution options here for click-through.

238
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:05,280
It's 1-day click or 7-day click.

239
00:23:05,340 --> 00:23:08,600
There are some brands that we have seen run 1-day click,

240
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:14,700
but I would not suggest running 1-day click unless you are spending above 20 or $30,000 a day on ads,

241
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:17,400
cuz there's just really not a point in doing so.

242
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:21,420
And even then, we still recommend for most brands to just to run 7-day click,

243
00:23:21,420 --> 00:23:28,740
to get data into the account and just make sure that you're getting the best data for Meta and giving it a chance to actually

244
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:33,500
find people who maybe won't purchase right away, but will purchase over that 7-day window.

245
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:38,800
Now, a bit of a newer attribution model that Meta has implemented is engaged video view.

246
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:44,280
And as you can see here, what engaged view means is when someone views your ad and takes action within 1 day.

247
00:23:44,440 --> 00:23:49,880
For images, engaged views are counted when an image is visible at least 50% of the screen for 2 seconds.

248
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:58,020
For videos, engaged views are counted when a video is played for at least 10 seconds or for 97% of its total length, if it's shorter than 10 seconds.

249
00:23:58,240 --> 00:24:05,120
will learn from your engaged-view conversions and show your ads to people likely to engage view within the same period. Engaged view is

250
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:12,100
available for all placements except Facebook in-stream video ads, which cannot be skipped." And so this is something new that Meta has

251
00:24:12,100 --> 00:24:19,660
implemented due to some of the flaws that typical view-through attribution has. And for about 90% of the brands that we work with right now,

252
00:24:19,660 --> 00:24:26,320
we actually don't run any view-through attribution. So, what we would actually run for our brands is just 7-day click only,

253
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:34,420
so we would not select any view-through attribution. But with this new engaged-view, we have been testing this, because what this is is a bit of a better

254
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:41,180
view-through attribution, because what happens a lot with standard view-through attribution if you are at more scale, okay? So,

255
00:24:41,180 --> 00:24:47,920
most of the brands that we work with are spending around six figures or more per month on Meta, and so what happens here is Meta

256
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:54,640
takes low-hanging fruit, okay? And especially for some of our brands that have supplements or have high repeat-customer purchases,

257
00:24:54,960 --> 00:25:01,760
Meta is just going to again try to get, as we go back into the campaign level, the highest volume of purchases

258
00:25:01,760 --> 00:25:08,400
at the lowest cost for your business. And so if it has the ability to get attribution

259
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:17,000
or to get you a high volume of purchases from people who just view your video or view your ad, a lot of the times it's going to do that,

260
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:24,920
okay? We have seen at times, and if you want more information on this, I again actually have another video on my channel that talks about how to understand

261
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:31,360
and how to pick attribution for your business, but we have seen at times Meta reporting like 7 to 10x return on ad spend,

262
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:37,660
but when you actually break down the attribution, you can see it's actually only like a 2 to 3x return on ad spend, which is still really good,

263
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:45,120
but that's because a lot of it is view-through. So, if you are a brand that is just starting out, spending less than $1,000 a day, and you do not have,

